## 13. User Registration & Onboarding

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Browser
    participant UI
    participant Auth as Passport Auth
    participant GH as GitHub OAuth
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant Session
    participant Email

    User->>Browser: Visit Peer Platform
    Browser->>UI: GET /
    UI->>Browser: Show Landing Page
    
    User->>Browser: Click "Login with GitHub"
    Browser->>UI: GET /auth/github
    UI->>Auth: Initiate OAuth
    Auth->>GH: Redirect to GitHub OAuth
    
    GH->>User: Show Authorization Page
    Note over GH,User: User Reviews Permissions:<br/>- Read email<br/>- Read profile
    
    User->>GH: Click "Authorize"
    GH->>Auth: Callback with Authorization Code
    Auth->>GH: Exchange Code for Access Token
    GH-->>Auth: Access Token + Refresh Token
    
    Auth->>GH: GET /user (Fetch Profile)
    GH-->>Auth: User Profile Data
    
    Auth->>DB: findOne({githubId})
    
    alt User Exists
        DB-->>Auth: User Found
        Auth->>DB: Update lastLogin, avatarUrl
    else New User
        DB-->>Auth: User Not Found
        Auth->>DB: Create New User Record
        Note over DB: Default Values:<br/>- subscription: 'free'<br/>- tokenQuota: 1000<br/>- tokensUsed: 0
        
        Auth->>Email: Send Welcome Email
        Email-->>User: Welcome Email with Guide
    end
    
    Auth->>Session: Create Session
    Session-->>Auth: Session ID
    Auth->>Browser: Set Session Cookie (httpOnly, secure)
    
    Browser->>UI: Redirect to /dashboard
    UI->>DB: Fetch User Data
    UI->>DB: Fetch User's Installations
    UI->>DB: Fetch Recent PRRuns
    
    DB-->>UI: Dashboard Data
    UI->>Browser: Render Dashboard
    Browser-->>User: Show Personalized Dashboard
```

---

## 14. GitHub App Installation & Configuration

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant GH as GitHub
    participant API
    participant DB
    participant Encrypt as Encryption Service

    User->>GH: Navigate to Peer App Page
    User->>GH: Click "Install" or "Configure"
    
    GH->>User: Select Organization/Account
    User->>GH: Choose Account
    
    GH->>User: Select Repositories
    Note over GH,User: Options:<br/>- All repositories<br/>- Only select repositories
    
    User->>GH: Select Repos & Click "Install"
    
    GH->>API: POST /webhook/github-app
    Note over GH,API: Event: installation.created
    
    API->>API: Verify Webhook Signature<br/>(HMAC SHA-256)
    
    alt Signature Invalid
        API-->>GH: 401 Unauthorized
    else Signature Valid
        API->>API: Parse Installation Data
        
        API->>DB: Create Installation Record
        Note over DB: Installation Data:<br/>- installationId<br/>- account (org/user)<br/>- repositories[]<br/>- permissions{}
        
        API->>GH: Create Installation Token<br/>POST /app/installations/:id/access_tokens
        GH-->>API: Installation Token (1 hour expiry)
        
        API->>Encrypt: Encrypt Token
        Encrypt-->>API: Encrypted Token
        
        API->>DB: Save Encrypted Token
        
        API->>GH: Get Repository List<br/>GET /installation/repositories
        GH-->>API: Repository Details
        
        API->>DB: Update Installation with Repos
        
        API->>DB: Set Default Config
        Note over DB: Default Settings:<br/>- mode: 'comment'<br/>- autoMerge: false<br/>- autofix: true
        
        API-->>GH: 200 OK
        
        API->>DB: Check if User Exists for Account
        
        alt User Not Found
            API->>DB: Create Placeholder User
            Note over DB: Will be linked when<br/>user logs in
        end
        
        GH-->>User: Installation Success
    end
    
    User->>GH: Redirect to Setup URL
    GH->>API: GET /installations/:id/setup
    API->>User: Show Configuration Page
    
    User->>API: Configure Settings
    Note over User,API: Settings:<br/>- Enable/Disable Autofix<br/>- Auto-merge preference<br/>- Notification settings
    
    API->>DB: Update Installation Config
    DB-->>API: Success
    API-->>User: Configuration Saved
```

